checkuser-uic-invalid-username-category:
{{tracking category name}}
Name of the [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Help:Tracking categories|tracking category]] where pages are listed that use the <code><nowiki>{{#uic:}}</nowiki></code> parser function with a value that cannot be the name of a registered user and is not an IP address.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-uic-invalid-username-category-desc}}

checkuser-uic-invalid-username-category-:
Description of the tracking category for invalid <code><nowiki>{{#uic:}}</nowiki></code> targets. Shown on [[Special:TrackingCategories]].

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-uic-invalid-username-category}}

checkuser-uic-ip-target-category:
{{tracking category name}}
Name of the [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Help:Tracking categories|tracking category]] where pages are listed that use the <code><nowiki>{{#uic:}}</nowiki></code> parser function with an IP address or range.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-uic-ip-target-category-desc}}

checkuser-uic-ip-target-category-desc:
Description of the tracking category for <code><nowiki>{{#uic:}}</nowiki></code> with IP targets. Shown on [[Special:TrackingCategories]].

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-uic-ip-target-category}}

checkuser-userinfocard-copy-username-but:
Aria label and tooltip for the button in the user info card header that copies the user name to the clipboard.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-userinfocard-copy-username-copied}}

checkuser-userinfocard-copy-username-cop:
Aria label and tooltip shown on the copy button in the user info card header once the user name has been copied to the clipboard, until the pointer leaves the header.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|checkuser-userinfocard-copy-username-button-aria-label}}

checkuser-userinfocard-count-exceeds-max:
{{optional}}
{{identical|$1+}}

Displayed in the UserInfoCard when a numeric value exceeds a configurable limit (by default 1000).

Parameters:
* $1 - The maximum number that can be displayed. This is followed by a plus sign to indicate that the actual count is larger.
